-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ג/6 (16.2.2023): עדכון תוספת שקלית 2016 לעובדי הוראה
-- בחטיבה העליונה ובכיתות יג'-יד' ועדכון תוספת 87 מעבר לרפורמה למנהלים בעוז לתמורה.
-- The index update of two shekel supplements from 1.1.2023: who is
-- covered, the amounts, and when the owners pay the principals' one.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

-- Time in this file is counted in salary MONTHS from December 2022
-- (month 0): January 2023 is 1, February 2023 is 2.
`January 2023`  MEANS 1
`February 2023` MEANS 2

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ג/6`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, date, reference number, circular number, addressee (the owners of educational institutions), greeting and subject line; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p13 The sources: the wage agreements of 14.3.2018 (§§5א(ב), 5ב(ב)) and 23.3.2017 (§4ד) and circular תשפ"ב/4 — the 2016 shekel supplement is linked to the consumer price index; the amounts below carry it.
-- akn:preamble/p14 The circular's purpose: to publish the index update of the 2016 shekel supplement from 1.1.2023; the update itself is section א.

§§ `Indexation`

-- ¶15: the supplement is linked to the December 2022 index (published in
-- January 2023) against the December 2020 index (published in January
-- 2021). The circular prints neither index nor the agreed base amount, so
-- both are inputs; the amounts it prints in section א are data below.
@ref akn:preamble/p15
GIVEN `amount at the base index` IS A NUMBER @desc the supplement's amount as the agreements set it at the December 2020 index (not printed in this circular)
      `index of December 2022`  IS A NUMBER @desc the consumer price index for December 2022, published in January 2023
      `index of December 2020`  IS A NUMBER @desc the consumer price index for December 2020, published in January 2021
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the indexed amount` `amount at the base index` `index of December 2022` `index of December 2020` IS
    `amount at the base index` TIMES (`index of December 2022` DIVIDED BY `index of December 2020`)

§§ `Application`

@desc A teaching employee, as far as this circular asks about one.
DECLARE `circular 6 employee` HAS
    `graded in the teaching employees' grading`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by an owner of a supervised institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the employer owns an educational institution supervised by the Ministry of Education
    `employed in the upper division or grades 13-14` IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed in a חטיבה עליונה or in classes יג'-יד'
    `employed under the Oz LaTmura reform`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a principal`                                 IS A BOOLEAN

-- ¶16 defines "עובד הוראה" for the circular and limits it to the upper
-- division and grades 13-14; ¶17: under Oz LaTmura and outside it alike.
@ref akn:preamble/p16 akn:preamble/p17
GIVEN e IS A `circular 6 employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the circular applies to` e IF
        e's `graded in the teaching employees' grading`
    AND e's `employed by an owner of a supervised institution`
    AND e's `employed in the upper division or grades 13-14`

§§ `א. עדכון תוספת שקלית 2016`

@desc A printed amount of the 2016 shekel supplement: the group it is paid to, the monthly amount from 1.1.2023, and the amount it replaces.
DECLARE `shekel supplement row` HAS
    `row group`        IS A `supplement group`
    `amount from January 2023` IS A NUMBER
    `amount it replaces`       IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `supplement group` IS ONE OF
    `teachers in Oz LaTmura`
    `teachers not in Oz LaTmura, and principals`

-- ¶1-¶3 as printed, in shekels a month, from 1.1.2023.
@ref akn:art_a/p1 akn:art_a/p2 akn:art_a/p3
`the 2016 shekel supplement from 1.1.2023` MEANS
    LIST `shekel supplement row` `teachers in Oz LaTmura`                     1509.98 1433.98,
         `shekel supplement row` `teachers not in Oz LaTmura, and principals` 1276.85 1212.59

-- F-2022-23_tashpag_06-a: ¶3 "מורים שאינם ברפורמת עוז לתמורה ומנהלים" is
-- read with "not in Oz LaTmura" qualifying the teachers only, so EVERY
-- principal falls in the second group, in the reform or not.
GIVEN e IS A `circular 6 employee`
GIVETH A `supplement group`
DECIDE `the group of` e IS
    IF e's `is a principal`
    THEN `teachers not in Oz LaTmura, and principals`
    ELSE IF e's `employed under the Oz LaTmura reform`
         THEN `teachers in Oz LaTmura`
         ELSE `teachers not in Oz LaTmura, and principals`

GIVEN g IS A `supplement group`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the printed amount for` g IS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `amount from January 2023`)
             (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row group` EQUALS g) `the 2016 shekel supplement from 1.1.2023`))

@export The monthly 2016 shekel supplement (תוספת שקלית 2016) a teaching employee in the upper division or grades 13-14 is owed from 1 January 2023 under circular תשפ"ג/6; 0 outside the circular's scope
GIVEN e IS A `circular 6 employee` @desc the employee
      `month` IS A NUMBER @desc the salary month, counted from December 2022 (January 2023 = 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `2016 shekel supplement` e `month` IS
    IF `the circular applies to` e AND `month` AT LEAST `January 2023`
    THEN `the printed amount for` (`the group of` e)
    ELSE 0

-- F-2022-23_tashpag_06-a: under the other reading the qualifier governs
-- "ומנהלים" too, and a principal in Oz LaTmura is in the second group only
-- if he is not in the reform — i.e. never; he then falls in the first group
-- if a principal is a "מורה", or in no group. Either way his amount differs.
`a principal in Oz LaTmura` MEANS
    `circular 6 employee` WITH
        `graded in the teaching employees' grading`      IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner of a supervised institution` IS TRUE
        `employed in the upper division or grades 13-14` IS TRUE
        `employed under the Oz LaTmura reform`           IS TRUE
        `is a principal`                                 IS TRUE

GIVEN e IS A `circular 6 employee`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the amounts if the qualifier also governs principals, principals counted as teachers` e IS
    IF e's `employed under the Oz LaTmura reform`
    THEN LIST (`the printed amount for` `teachers in Oz LaTmura`)
    ELSE LIST (`the printed amount for` `teachers not in Oz LaTmura, and principals`)

`the readings of ¶3 pay a principal in Oz LaTmura differently` MEANS
    NOT (`the amounts if the qualifier also governs principals, principals counted as teachers` `a principal in Oz LaTmura`
         EQUALS LIST (`2016 shekel supplement` `a principal in Oz LaTmura` `January 2023`))
#ASSERT `the readings of ¶3 pay a principal in Oz LaTmura differently`

-- ¶4: the Ministry reimburses the owners for the 2016 supplement through the hour costs.
@ref akn:art_a/p4
`how the owners are reimbursed for the 2016 shekel supplement` MEANS
    `the relevant hour costs in the payments system`

DECLARE `reimbursement channel` IS ONE OF
    `the relevant hour costs in the payments system`
    `the payments system under subject 558`

§§ `ב. עדכון סכום תוספת 87 מעבר רפורמה למנהלים`

-- ¶1: per the agreement and section 18 of circular תשע"ח/9, the 87
-- transition supplement of principals employed under Oz LaTmura is updated
-- by the index update above; ¶2 prints the amount.
@ref akn:art_b/p1
GIVEN e IS A `circular 6 employee`
      `amount before the update` IS A NUMBER @desc the principal's 87 transition supplement at the December 2020 index
      `index of December 2022`   IS A NUMBER
      `index of December 2020`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 87 transition supplement updated by the index` e `amount before the update` `index of December 2022` `index of December 2020` IS
    IF `entitled to the updated 87 transition supplement` e
    THEN `the indexed amount` `amount before the update` `index of December 2022` `index of December 2020`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN e IS A `circular 6 employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the updated 87 transition supplement` e IF
        `the circular applies to` e
    AND e's `is a principal`
    AND e's `employed under the Oz LaTmura reform`

@ref akn:art_b/p2
`the 87 transition supplement from 1.1.2023` MEANS 1101.60
`the 87 transition supplement it replaces`    MEANS 1046.15

@export The monthly '87 transition-to-reform supplement (תוספת 87 מעבר לרפורמה) of a principal under Oz LaTmura from 1 January 2023 under circular תשפ"ג/6; 0 for anyone else
GIVEN e IS A `circular 6 employee` @desc the employee
      `month` IS A NUMBER @desc the salary month, counted from December 2022 (January 2023 = 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `87 transition supplement` e `month` IS
    IF `entitled to the updated 87 transition supplement` e AND `month` AT LEAST `January 2023`
    THEN `the 87 transition supplement from 1.1.2023`
    ELSE 0

-- ¶3: paid from January 2023's salary and no later than February 2023's,
-- with retroactive differences for January.
@ref akn:art_b/p3
GIVEN e IS A `circular 6 employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `circular 6 action`
DECIDE `payment of the updated 87 supplement` e IS
    IF `entitled to the updated 87 transition supplement` e
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `pay the updated 87 supplement with January's differences` `paid for January`
               PROVIDED `paid for January` AT LEAST `87 transition supplement` e `January 2023`
         WITHIN `February 2023`
         LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ג/6 ב: the updated supplement is paid no later than February 2023's salary, with January's differences"
    ELSE FULFILLED

DECLARE `circular 6 action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the updated 87 supplement with January's differences` HAS `amount for January` IS A NUMBER

-- ¶4: the reimbursement for the 87 supplement runs under subject 558.
@ref akn:art_b/p4
`how the owners are reimbursed for the 87 transition supplement` MEANS
    `the payments system under subject 558`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off, the signatories and the list of copies; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- The employees are made up; the amounts are the circular's.
`an Oz LaTmura teacher in the upper division` MEANS
    `circular 6 employee` WITH
        `graded in the teaching employees' grading`      IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner of a supervised institution` IS TRUE
        `employed in the upper division or grades 13-14` IS TRUE
        `employed under the Oz LaTmura reform`           IS TRUE
        `is a principal`                                 IS FALSE

`a teacher outside the reform in grades 13-14` MEANS
    `circular 6 employee` WITH
        `graded in the teaching employees' grading`      IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner of a supervised institution` IS TRUE
        `employed in the upper division or grades 13-14` IS TRUE
        `employed under the Oz LaTmura reform`           IS FALSE
        `is a principal`                                 IS FALSE

`a middle-school teacher` MEANS
    `circular 6 employee` WITH
        `graded in the teaching employees' grading`      IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner of a supervised institution` IS TRUE
        `employed in the upper division or grades 13-14` IS FALSE
        `employed under the Oz LaTmura reform`           IS TRUE
        `is a principal`                                 IS FALSE

#ASSERT `2016 shekel supplement` `an Oz LaTmura teacher in the upper division` `January 2023` EQUALS 1509.98
#ASSERT `2016 shekel supplement` `a teacher outside the reform in grades 13-14` `February 2023` EQUALS 1276.85
#ASSERT `2016 shekel supplement` `a principal in Oz LaTmura` `January 2023` EQUALS 1276.85
#ASSERT `2016 shekel supplement` `a middle-school teacher` `January 2023` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `87 transition supplement` `a principal in Oz LaTmura` `January 2023` EQUALS 1101.60
#ASSERT `87 transition supplement` `an Oz LaTmura teacher in the upper division` `January 2023` EQUALS 0

-- The three printed updates are one index step: each new amount over its
-- old one is 1.053 to three decimals (5.3%, the December 2021 → December
-- 2022 change the previous update had not yet carried).
GIVEN `old amount` IS A NUMBER, `new amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the old amount indexed by 5.3%` `old amount` `new amount` IF
        `new amount` DIVIDED BY `old amount` AT LEAST 1.0525
    AND `new amount` DIVIDED BY `old amount` LESS THAN 1.0535

#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD `is the old amount indexed by 5.3%` (r's `amount it replaces`) (r's `amount from January 2023`))
            `the 2016 shekel supplement from 1.1.2023`
#ASSERT `is the old amount indexed by 5.3%` `the 87 transition supplement it replaces` `the 87 transition supplement from 1.1.2023`

-- Paid in February with January's differences: fulfilled. Not paid by
-- the end of February: breached.
#TRACE `payment of the updated 87 supplement` `a principal in Oz LaTmura` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the updated 87 supplement with January's differences` 1101.60 AT 2
#TRACE `payment of the updated 87 supplement` `a principal in Oz LaTmura` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the updated 87 supplement with January's differences` 1046.15 AT 2
